---Git Hub Branching Stratagies---

main → Always production-ready
                  This branch always contains the stable and deployable version of the application.
develop → Integration branch where new features add
This is the default branch where developers integrate their completed features. 
Contains code that is tested internally but not yet ready for production.
feature/ → Short-lived development branches (per task)
 Every new feature or task gets its own branch, created from develop.
Once completed, a pull request (PR) is raised to merge into develop.
release/ → Created when preparing for a final release
    Created when the develop branch is ready for a release.
    Perform user testing (UAT )               
    Fix bugs found during testing  
    Prepare release notes  
    Update version numbers
hotfix/ → Emergency fixes on production
Created from the main branch when a critical production issue occurs.
Used to patch production without waiting for the next release cycle.
Once fixed:
Merged back into main (to deploy immediately)
Merged into develop (so future versions contain the fix)


