--->>S3 Storage Classes
Answer:
🔹 S3 Standard
Used for frequently accessed data like applications, websites, or active files. It provides high availability and low latency across multiple Availability Zones.
🔹 S3 Intelligent-Tiering
Used when access patterns are unpredictable. It automatically moves data between tiers to optimize cost without affecting performance.
🔹 S3 Standard-IA (Infrequent Access)
Used for data that is accessed less often, such as backups. It has lower storage cost but includes a retrieval fee.
🔹 S3 One Zone-IA
Similar to Standard-IA but stores data in a single Availability Zone, making it cheaper but less resilient.
🔹 S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval
Used for archival data that still needs immediate access, with lower cost than Standard classes.
🔹 S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval
Used for long-term backups where retrieval can take minutes to hours, offering lower storage cost.
🔹 S3 Glacier Deep Archive
Cheapest storage class, used for long-term archival or compliance data where retrieval can take 12 hours or more.

